# Docker Development & Execution Standards

1. **Hot-Reloading (Debug Mode):** Configure Dockerfiles and volumes so that any code updates in backend or frontend instantly trigger a project reload without rebuilding the container. Ensure that any database model modifications are easily reflected in Alembic tracking.

2. **Automated Migrations:** All pending database migrations must run and apply to the database automatically immediately after the project reloads/starts.

3. **Unified Execution:** A single `docker-compose.local.yml` file located at the project root must launch both backend and frontend services simultaneously.

4. **Container Idempotency:** Subsequent executions of the `docker-compose up` command must reuse existing layers, cached volumes, and containers. Prevent image re-construction or container duplication unless explicit changes to the configuration are made.

## LLM Provider Strategy

The backend **auto-selects** the LLM provider at startup (`ml/llm_service.py`):

| Condition | Provider | Models |
|---|---|---|
| `GROQ_API_KEY` set in `.env` | **Groq** (cloud, LPU-fast) | `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` + `llama-3.1-8b-instant` |
| No key | **Ollama** (local fallback) | `llama3.2` + `llama3.2:1b` |

**Groq (recommended):** Set `GROQ_API_KEY` in `.env`. The `ollama` service in docker-compose is optional — the backend no longer depends on it when Groq is active.

**Ollama (local fallback):** Remove `GROQ_API_KEY` from `.env`. The `ollama` service in docker-compose starts and pulls both models via `ci_cd/ollama/entrypoint.sh`.

## Running Tests Inside Docker

```bash
# Unit + integration tests (fast, mocked externals):
docker compose -f docker-compose.local.yml exec backend pytest

# Behavioral RAG tests (real Ollama + Qdrant, ~1 min):
docker compose -f docker-compose.local.yml exec backend pytest -m behavioral -v

# Full Ragas eval (slow, ~20 min):
docker compose -f docker-compose.local.yml exec -e RUN_EVAL_TESTS=1 backend pytest -m eval -v
```

## Alembic Migrations

Run from inside the backend container (alembic.ini is in `/app/backend/`):
```bash
docker compose exec backend bash -c "cd /app && alembic -c /app/backend/alembic.ini upgrade head"
```